  "description": "High-performance Go library for reading, writing, and processing DICOM medical image files. Supports parsing of multi-frame imagery (encapsulated and native pixel data), channel-based streaming of image frames during parse, writing datasets back to DICOM, JSON-serialisable dataset and element representations, and flat iteration over nested sequences. Ships a CLI tool (dicomutil) for extracting imagery and metadata without writing code. The reference DICOM library for the Go ecosystem — a ground-up rewrite of the originally unmaintained go-dicom, now at v1.x stable with 1.1k GitHub stars.",
